WEBVTT

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:09.779
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the fourth. Everyone on? I've got a frozen picture but I can hear you.</v>

00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:17.140
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'm here. The heating in the portakabin's still making it feel like August. Lovely in June, that.</v>

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:26.510
<v Tomasz Nowak>Better than outside. Whose new car is that in the car park, then? Taking up rather a lot of space.</v>

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:30.789
<v Callum Reid>Not mine. Mine's the one held together by road dirt.</v>

00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:41.579
<v Sarah Okafor>And the broken coffee machine in the canteen means we're doing this without proper coffee. Just moaning, not putting it on the maintenance list.</v>

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:47.170
<v Priya Raman>Good, because I'm not qualified to deal with that level of emergency.</v>

00:00:49.609 --> 00:00:53.109
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, um, completed stuff first. Then what we're actually agreeing.</v>

00:00:53.469 --> 00:00:59.420
<v David Whitfield>I signed off the inspection on the WHB on Tuesday. That's finished, nothing carrying over from it.</v>

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:08.010
<v Fiona Doyle>And we finished the repair on the turbine one compressor last night. That's closed on the plan now.</v>

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.890
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Both done, neither needs another job raising.</v>

00:01:13.719 --> 00:01:20.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>Still waiting on parts for the 11kV board, nothing we can do until they arrive. No progress to report there.</v>

00:01:21.319 --> 00:01:24.819
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, understood. Still blocked, not something we're picking up today.</v>

00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:34.159
<v Callum Reid>Same story for access: can't get to the line 1 TCU until production gives us a window. We haven't got that window.</v>

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.069
<v Fiona Doyle>That's staying blocked, then. Not in today's available work.</v>

00:01:38.459 --> 00:01:44.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Also, the shutdown on the palletiser is cancelled now, production need it running. That shutdown's off.</v>

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:48.920
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, the planned shutdown. Not permission to run through a fault, obviously.</v>

00:01:51.189 --> 00:02:00.640
<v David Whitfield>While we're there, I noticed the Palletiser was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just an observation, not asking for a temperature job.</v>

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:08.219
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, so the jam on the Palletiser is separate from that. That's the live issue, not the warmth.</v>

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. What's the position with that jam, then?</v>

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:22.919
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser by 11am. Normal priority. That's a local fault intervention, not bringing the cancelled shutdown back.</v>

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.780
<v Fiona Doyle>Olu for the Palletiser, by 11am, normal priority. Got you.</v>

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:31.580
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, that's mine. Safe isolation for the jam, obviously.</v>

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:36.710
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that's understood. I was talking about the longer shutdown, not skipping isolation.</v>

00:02:38.139 --> 00:02:43.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz Nowak, can you grease and check the bearings on the turbine two for Monday?</v>

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:51.349
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'll grease and check the bearings on the turbine two for Monday. I can take that.</v>

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.319
<v David Whitfield>Grease and condition check, rather than a strip-down?</v>

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:01.969
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's it. Grease and check the bearings. Not agreeing a strip-down here.</v>

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Monday against Tomasz Nowak. Fine.</v>

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:11.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, water side next. There are two separate things here, so don't roll them into one.</v>

00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:20.169
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll take vibration readings on the water booster by 11am. Low priority, but I'll have the readings done by then.</v>

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:26.430
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah for the water booster readings. That's not you taking the pressure-drop investigation as well?</v>

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:31.159
<v Sarah Okafor>No, just the vibration readings. Keep the pressure-drop investigation separate.</v>

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:39.009
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, the pressure drop on the Water Booster Pump still needs investigating. The readings aren't a substitute for that.</v>

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:50.250
<v Sarah Okafor>We need someone to investigate the pressure drop on the Water Booster Pump after lunch. Drop everything for that one. Who can actually take it?</v>

00:03:52.289 --> 00:03:54.740
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, I can't commit to that one.</v>

00:03:55.919 --> 00:03:58.370
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not me either. I can't accept it.</v>

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.159
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, no, I can't take ownership of that.</v>

00:04:03.319 --> 00:04:08.569
<v David Whitfield>I'm flagging it, but I'm not taking it on. Don't put my name against it.</v>

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.400
<v Callum Reid>No taker from me either, I'm afraid.</v>

00:04:13.949 --> 00:04:18.500
<v Fiona Doyle>Then it's unallocated. After lunch, drop everything for that one, but no owner.</v>

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:25.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. It's still needed and still that urgent. Nobody's accepted it; we're not pretending it's covered.</v>

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:34.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Separately, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve after lunch. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:40.180
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Okay, Saz on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve sensors. Calibration, yeah?</v>

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, recalibrate the sensors. That's the job I'm taking after lunch.</v>

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.220
<v David Whitfield>Right, not a mechanical valve overhaul. Different scope.</v>

00:04:51.529 --> 00:04:56.779
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it: Saz, sensor recalibration after lunch. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:06.129
<v Priya Raman>While we're on the less dramatic stuff, I'll sort the training records for the new starters by end of day. No rush.</v>

00:05:07.839 --> 00:05:11.339
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, PR. Training records with you, by end of day.</v>

00:05:13.649 --> 00:05:18.199
<v Priya Raman>Yep. No rush, but I am taking it, not just mentioning the pile.</v>

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:24.800
<v Fiona Doyle>Paperwork doesn't make much noise, does it? Still manages to fill a stand-up.</v>

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:30.139
<v Priya Raman>Usually just me sighing at it, to be fair.</v>

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:34.639
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll run the monthly fire alarm test by the 28th.</v>

00:05:35.009 --> 00:05:39.910
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah for the monthly fire alarm test, by the 28th. That's this month's one.</v>

00:05:41.569 --> 00:05:43.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, June's monthly test. Mine.</v>

00:05:44.139 --> 00:05:52.889
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, so I'll book a contractor to look at the CV01 by the end of the week. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:54.759 --> 00:06:01.060
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, talking over you—booking by the end of the week, not promising they'll actually be here by then?</v>

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:11.019
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. I'll get the contractor booked to look at the CV01 by the end of the week. That's the commitment, not a visit date.</v>

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:18.810
<v Fiona Doyle>Cal owns the booking. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. No contractor attendance date being agreed.</v>

00:06:19.629 --> 00:06:23.829
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. That's clear. Anything we've accidentally made sound available when it isn't?</v>

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:30.870
<v Tomasz Nowak>Only to underline the 11kV board is still parts-blocked. Nothing changed during this call.</v>

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, stays blocked. No new action on that.</v>

00:06:38.089 --> 00:06:42.639
<v Callum Reid>And line 1 TCU still has no production window. Same position as before.</v>

00:06:44.879 --> 00:06:51.529
<v Fiona Doyle>The uncovered one is the Water Booster Pump pressure drop. It's still nobody against that, despite the after-lunch urgency.</v>

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:59.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. Nobody assigned, nobody volunteered. Keep that visible as unallocated, not agreed to me alongside the readings.</v>

00:07:00.399 --> 00:07:04.600
<v Priya Raman>Right. And the coffee machine remains a source of emotional damage only.</v>

00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:07.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Cheers, everyone. That's us.</v>
